# nr-office-design-docx: what the wiring applies for the docx design expansion of the crate mixdog-office-design.
# (No protocol rows, no daemon service, no SERVICE_PENDING change, no Cargo edge: the module is pure and uses only
# dependencies the crate already has - mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, serde_json. It has no caller yet.)

# 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-design/src/lib.rs: in the list of modules, after the line `pub mod discipline;`
#    (keep the list sorted), add
pub mod docx;
#    and in the crate doc comment, after the sentence ending "... and the one reading of a preset table (`table_input`).",
#    add: "The docx design expansion (`docx`) turns a compose_document operation into the portable docx operations the
#    docx writer consumes."
#    Nothing else of lib.rs changes: the module reads the crate-private helpers `prop`, `opt_prop`, `text`, `text_of`,
#    `first_text`, `first_truthy` and `array_of` that lib.rs already defines.

# 2. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json, "sets" (keep the list sorted by set name; after "office-discipline"):
    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-docx.mjs --tree <tree>",
