# 3. For the later tasks of the track (nr-office-design-composition, -xlsx, -library, and the docx writer's caller):
#    the module exports
#      docx::expand_docx_document(operation, design, &mut DocxState, composition: Option<&Value>) -> Result<Vec<Value>, String>
#        (design: a resolved design (only tokens.typography, tokens.colors and format are read); composition: the plan of
#         the composition system (only its id is read); DocxState { paragraph, table } is the counter Node's docxState is,
#         one per design request, shared by every compose_document of it);
#      docx::typography::{korean_design, document_typography, pair_table_east_asia, is_serif_face, has_hangul}
#        (korean_design is what the xlsx composer calls for a Korean sheet);
#      docx::components::{add_docx_decision_callout, add_docx_metric_strip, add_docx_roadmap, add_docx_section_table, CalloutOptions}.
#    The table widths of a plain section table are left absent in the operations (Node does the same): the docx writer
#    takes them from mixdog_office_base::column_widths::natural_column_widths when it writes the file.
